name: Request
type: Coordination/Message
description: >
  A Message that solicits an answer. It establishes the expectation that the
  participant addressed by recipientChannel, or a suitable participant at the
  table when recipientChannel is absent, may eventually send a Response whose
  inResponseTo points to this Request. A Request may itself answer another
  Message, such as a counter-offer or clarifying question. Concrete request
  types define their payload and domain-specific recipient semantics.
